       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum prescription dose of 3,200 mg/day. The single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nDid you mean one of these common regimens?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), for mild to moderate pain\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common regimen for inflammatory conditions\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum, for short-term use only\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that. I'd suggest adding a note with your rationale."
